# Baseline wp dist-archive exclusions, adapted for team51-plugin-scaffold.
# wp dist-archive walks the disk (not git), so vendor/ and freshly built
# block/asset output are included automatically; this file removes
# everything else that must not ship in the release zip.
#
# Patterns follow gitignore semantics: a bare name (no slash) matches at
# any depth, a leading `/` anchors to the repo root. `/build` is root-
# anchored on purpose — it excludes only the top-level build/ directory
# (Infection mutation-testing logs), while blocks/build and the
# assets/*/build directories (compiled block and script output) are left
# alone and ship in the archive.

.git*
.superpowers
.idea
.vscode
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.distignore
node_modules
tests
changelog
bin
/build
vendor/bin
*.dist.xml
.wp-env*.json
.phpcs.xml
.phpcs.tests.xml
.phpstan.neon
.composer-require-checker.json
infection.json
playwright.config.js
postcss.config.js
.editorconfig
package*.json
composer.json
composer.lock
README.scaffold.md

# Secret material — never ship, even if a consumer forgets to list it.
# .pem/.key are root-anchored (leading /) so certs bundled under vendor/
# (e.g. CA bundles) still ship.
.env*
/*.pem
/*.key
id_rsa*
.npmrc
auth.json
